cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FISH: Function-level Inspection of Scheduling Hierarchies"
message: >-
  If you use FISH in academic work, please cite the paper
  given under preferred-citation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tasyaran
    given-names: Fatih
    email: fatihtasyaran@sabanciuniv.edu
repository-code: "https://github.com/FatihTasyaran/FISH_INTERFERE"
abstract: >-
  FISH is a profiling framework for ROS 2 + GPU workloads. It captures
  LTTng kernel/userspace traces, NVIDIA Nsight Systems GPU profiling
  data, and system-state snapshots from inside the container where the
  target ROS 2 nodes run, then reconstructs a typed task-graph
  (executors -> nodes -> entities -> callbacks -> GPU kernels) and
  exports it for analysis and visualisation.
keywords:
  - ros2
  - profiling
  - lttng
  - nsight-systems
  - task-graph
  - real-time
  - gpu
license: MIT
